hey this is presh talwalkar reminding  you to mind your decisions  simplify and prove your answer to the  following expression you're not allowed  to use calculators or computers  i received many email requests for this  type of problem i think akshat in india  for suggesting it to me first  can you figure it out  give this problem a try and when you're  ready keep watching the video for a  solution  so how can we simplify this expression  i'll first write a as the number that's  under the first cube root and then b  will be a square root conjugate that's  under the second cube root  notice that the cube root of a is a real  number and the cube root of b is a real  number so their sum will also be a real  number so in the end we're looking for a  real number  now we'll set this entire expression  which is the cube root of a plus the  cube root of b  we'll set that equal to x  now we'll cube both sides  and then we'll expand  now let's simplify this expression  we'll first put the squares inside of  these cube roots  now we'll group these cube roots  together  we can then write a squared as a a and b  squared as bb  notice we have an a b term here and a ba  term here and they'll be equal to each  other  what's the product of square root  conjugates  the nice thing is it will be a  difference of squares and this  simplifies to be negative five cubed  we'll substitute that in  and now  negative 5 cubed if we take the cube  root of that we end up with negative 5.  3 times negative 5 is equal to negative  15.  so we then have negative 15 and we can  group the remaining terms which will be  the cube root of a plus the cube root of  b  we now recall that x was defined to be  exactly this quantity so we can  substitute that in  now a plus b  will be equal to just 16 because the  square root terms will cancel  so we end up with a simple polynomial  expression  x cubed is equal to 16 minus 15x  if there's a solution in this equation  we're looking for a real value to be the  answer to our original expression  so we write x cubed plus 15x minus 16 is  equal to 0.  how can we solve this equation  well usually you can try special values  and you'll quickly see that x is equal  to 1 is a solution to this equation  consequently x minus 1 will be a factor  of this polynomial  so we can factor this into the following  product of x minus 1 and the quadratic x  squared plus x plus 16.  we can solve the quadratic using the  quadratic formula  but we'll learn that the quadratic roots  both involve non-zero imaginary parts so  they're extraneous roots they can't be  the answer to our original problem  because we're looking for a real value  of x  this means the answer is x is equal to  one  wow this is a most unexpected answer for  a simple algebra problem  now you might double check this exercise  by typing it in wolfram alpha  will it give the answer of one  you might surprisingly find that it  gives a complex answer with a non-zero  imaginary part  what's going on  well wolfram alpha is using the  principal root  the reason is the equation x cubed  equals c has three solutions  and wolfram alpha will take the  principal branch cut which is most  commonly used in higher mathematics  but we don't want the principal branch  cut we want the real valued root so how  can we force wolfram alpha to do that  there are a couple of ways  one is you can use the command of cube  root that in fact will give you the real  valued root and you will get the answer  one  and for other roots you can use the  command absurd of x comma n this will  give you the real nth root of x  it's a pretty neat problem  thanks for watching these math videos  available for free on youtube build  confidence for students and inspire  mathematical discovery for viewers  around the world they have over 100  million views and the channel has over 1  million subscribers please subscribe for  free to get the newest videos you can  email me a puzzle or math topic presh  mindyourdecisions